    "intro_narrative": "Welcome aboard the Aetherius, a marvel of clockwork and steam engineering that now drifts aimlessly through the smog-choked skies. The crew has vanished without a trace, leaving behind only the rhythmic ticking of cooling brass machinery and the ominous hiss of leaking steam pipes. The ship's altitude is dropping rapidly, and unless you can restart the primary boiler systems, it will crash into the jagged iron spires of the city below. Your ultimate goal is to retrieve the legendary Master Core, the mysterious heart of the ship's power grid, locked away securely in the deepest sector of the engine room. To survive, you must navigate a complex web of interconnected mechanical consoles, decipher ancient navigation logs, and reroute steam pressure through a series of logical validators. Every gear, dial, and lever on this ship is connected in a delicate chain of mechanical operations. Pay close attention to the flow of information between the devices. The clock is ticking, the atmospheric pressure is rising, and the Aetherius depends entirely on your intellect to fly once more.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
